The inotify calls without the Linux option (ADR 0615): their sysdep tags
and signatures leave the Linux option's block, so a system layer without
that option can implement them, and <abi-bits/inotify.h> no longer
refuses to be included without it. The Radix system layer builds the
Linux option's inotify_init, inotify_init1, inotify_add_watch and
inotify_rm_watch (options/linux/generic/sys-inotify.cpp) and installs its
<sys/inotify.h> (ports/mlibc/build.sh), which need nothing of Linux's and
nothing under the GPL: both files are mlibc's own, under the MIT license.

diff --git a/abis/linux/inotify.h b/abis/linux/inotify.h
--- a/abis/linux/inotify.h
+++ b/abis/linux/inotify.h
@@ -2,10 +2,6 @@
 #define _ABIBITS_INOTIFY_H
 
 #include <mlibc-config.h>
-
-#if !__MLIBC_LINUX_OPTION
-#  error "<sys/inotify.h> is inherently Linux specific. Enable the Linux option or do not use this header."
-#endif /* !__MLIBC_LINUX_OPTION */
 
 #include <abi-bits/fcntl.h>
 
diff --git a/options/internal/include/mlibc/sysdep-signatures.hpp b/options/internal/include/mlibc/sysdep-signatures.hpp
--- a/options/internal/include/mlibc/sysdep-signatures.hpp
+++ b/options/internal/include/mlibc/sysdep-signatures.hpp
@@ -295,9 +295,6 @@
